------- FILE main.asm
------- FILE bend.asm LEVEL 2 PASS 3
      0  239c					      include	"bend.asm"
      1  239c							; Fat Chip 64 - bends (SPACE / the keytar's buttons and wheel), v0.13
      2  239c							;
      3  239c							; What everything is bent by: m = 0-192 sixteenths of a semitone (an octave
      4  239c							; at most), up or down (bendMag, bendUp), from three things added together:
      5  239c							;   the BEND DOWN / BEND UP actions (SPACE or a keytar button, held): bendLvl
      6  239c							;     0-255 ramps up over about 1 s while held, back over about 0.5 s; full =
      7  239c							;     the menu's BEND RANGE (1-12 semitones, default 2)
      8  239c							;   the keytar's wheel: wheelMag 0-255 up or down, full = BEND RANGE
      9  239c							;   VINYL STOP (held): vinylLvl 0-255 the same way, like a record stopping:
     10  239c							;     speed (256 - lvl) / 256, the pitch 12 log2(1 / speed) down (vinPitch:
     11  239c							;     an octave by lvl 128). The SID keeps on down a second octave (vinSid)
     12  239c							;     and fades out from lvl 192; the beat and arp slow (up to 8x); at lvl
     13  239c							;     248 everything has stopped: silent, no drums (vinylCut). Let go, it
     14  239c							;     winds back up in 0.5 s.
     15  239c							; Then:
     16  239c							;   SID       its frequency x 2^(+-m/192), from tables (bendtab.asm)
     17  239c							;   Game Boy  bend range 12 (CC 85, sent with the sound), bend = 8192 +- m x 8192 / 192
     18  239c							;   MidiNES   p(n) x the table / 8192 for the triangle, twice for the pulses
     19  239c							;	       (p = the MidiNES triangle bend scale, 1710 at MIDI 36); notes
     20  239c							;	       without room at the bottom of the NES range don't bend down.
     21  239c							; Bends go out every BEND_TICK ms at most, and before each new NES note.
